# Testing Standards

Meridian uses Swift Package Manager for unit tests. All tests live in `MeridianTests/` and run via `swift test`.

## Before Every Build

Run tests before building in Xcode:

```bash
swift test
```

This catches logic regressions in seconds without launching the app. The test suite covers path detection, VDF parsing, window classification, bootstrap state machine, version comparison, and auth token handling.

## Test Architecture

### Why Inlined Logic (Mirror Pattern)

The `Meridian` target is an `executableTarget` in SPM. Swift does not support `@testable import` for executable targets (SE-0455 is still in draft as of March 2026). Tests therefore **inline copies of pure logic** from the production code.

### Mirror Contract

Every inlined function MUST have a comment identifying its production counterpart:

```swift
/// Mirror of WinePrefix.steamInstallDir
private func steamInstallDir(driveC: URL) -> URL { ... }
```

**WHENEVER you change logic in a production file, you MUST update the corresponding mirror in the test file.** Failing to do so allows tests to pass while production code is broken.

### What to Test

| Category | Examples | Test File |
|----------|----------|-----------|
| Path detection | `steamInstallDir`, `steamExeWindowsPath`, `steamLibraryFolders` | `WinePrefixTests.swift` |
| VDF parsing | `vdfKeyValue`, `hasSteamLoginSession`, `gameInstallDir` | `WinePrefixTests.swift` |
| File I/O round-trips | `writeLoginUsers` → `hasSteamLoginSession`, `ensureSteamCFG` idempotency | `WinePrefixTests.swift` |
| Window classification | Essential vs suppressible title patterns | `WindowClassificationTests.swift` |
| Bootstrap state machine | Phase transitions, retry cleanup decisions, quiescence detection | `BootstrapTests.swift` |
| Version comparison | Semver parsing, app vs engine tag classification | `AppUpdateCheckerTests.swift` |
| Auth token handling | RSA key construction, guard type mapping, VDF templates | `SteamCredentialAuthTests.swift` |
| Hash extraction | CDN path parsing, logo/capsule hash matching | `HashExtractionTests.swift` |
| Game install logic | ACF parsing, `isGameInstalled`, `isGameFullyInstalled`, `gameDownloadProgress`, install state machine | `GameInstallTests.swift` |

### What NOT to Test in Unit Tests

- Direct Wine process execution (use `Scripts/verify-bootstrap.sh` instead)
- Network calls to Steam API (use mock data or integration tests)
- Accessibility/AX framework calls (requires system permission)
- NSWorkspace process discovery (OS-dependent)

### CLI Testing for Game Compatibility

Before adding a game to `GameCompatibilityDB`, test it from CLI using the bundled engine only:

```bash
WINE64="$HOME/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/engine/wine/bin/wine64"
WINESERVER="$HOME/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/engine/wine/bin/wineserver"
WINEPREFIX="$HOME/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/bottles/steam/"
LIB="$HOME/Library/Application Support/com.meridian.app/engine/wine/lib"

export WINEPREFIX WINESERVER
export DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH="$LIB:$LIB/wine/x86_64-unix"

# 1. Install via SteamCMD
"$WINE64" "$WINEPREFIX/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamcmd.exe" \
  +login USERNAME +app_update APPID validate +quit

# 2. Launch directly
"$WINE64" "$WINEPREFIX/drive_c/Program Files (x86)/Steam/steamapps/common/GAMEDIR/game.exe" 2>&1 | head -50

# 3. Check for abort stubs
grep "aborting\|unimplemented function" /tmp/game-output.txt
```

Document results in GameCompatibilityDB even if the game works — this tracks verified titles.

## Test File Naming

```
MeridianTests/<ComponentName>Tests.swift
```

Examples: `BootstrapTests.swift`, `WindowClassificationTests.swift`, `WinePrefixTests.swift`

## Adding New Tests

1. Create the test file in `MeridianTests/`
2. Import `XCTest` (no `@testable import` — use mirror pattern)
3. Add a `MIRROR CONTRACT` comment block listing all mirrored functions
4. Write tests using temp directories for file I/O (clean up in `tearDown`)
5. Run `swift test` to verify
6. The SPM test target auto-discovers new files — no `Package.swift` changes needed

## Smoke Testing (Beyond Unit Tests)

For integration-level validation that requires the actual Wine engine:

```bash
# Full bootstrap smoke test (wipes prefix, installs Steam, verifies steamui.dll)
bash Scripts/verify-bootstrap.sh

# Bootstrap without wipe (faster, for iterating on fixes)
bash Scripts/verify-bootstrap.sh --no-wipe

# Run unit tests
swift test
```

## Regression Prevention Checklist

Before any PR or merge:

- [ ] `swift test` passes (all tests, including new ones for this change)
- [ ] No new `MeridianLog` categories without a matching entry in `logging-system.mdc`
- [ ] Bootstrap changes validated with `Scripts/verify-bootstrap.sh`
- [ ] Window pattern changes have corresponding `WindowClassificationTests` entries
- [ ] Auth changes have corresponding `SteamCredentialAuthTests` entries
